  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Lianchaifing hewei'Summit
    
    A leader within the Pinnacle, the splinter faction that broke from Qingfu'spire during the Aurora Stack succession crisis. Lianchaifing's significance rests almost entirely on a single act of institutional seizure executed with notable speed.
    
    When Ice-Crowned Shexuwohua fractured the Radiant Aurora-harp during a contested council session, Lianchaifing secured custody of the instrument within the hour — transit-wrapped and moved to the Aerie Perch vault before the session formally adjourned. No faction contested the claim. The Pinnacle possessed the only vault deep enough and membership disciplined enough to protect what the old council had demonstrably failed to protect. The justification writes itself, which is precisely what makes it worth scrutinizing.
    
    Lianchaifing subsequently reported the vault sealed, noting that the harp's three fracture lines caught stored light and threw shadows that moved without apparent source. She helped draft the custodial protocols that governed the harp's later use.
    
    When the Pinnacle mandated that all members hear the harp before swearing the coded greeting, Lianchaifing's delegation positioned the instrument in Light Ingjeizhi's central alcove at the conjunction of the third aurora-tide. She observed from the upper gallery — a vantage she chose, by her own account, because *when the harp was involved she watched faces, not light.* She catalogued every reaction to the faceless Xi's late arrival: who flinched, who straightened, who looked away with careful precision.
    
    An operative, then. The harp blessed a smuggler unbidden; Lianchaifing recorded who was disturbed by this and began calculating what it would cost.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771594600411_0", anchor: "secured custody of the instrument within the hour — transit-wrapped and moved to the Aerie Perch vault before the session formally adjourned", text: "Transit-wrapping an aurora artifact requires sanctified cloth cut to dimension, a minimum of two trained handlers, and — if the artifact is fractured and leaking stored light — a suppression lattice. None of these are items one has lying about on the off chance a council session goes badly. Lianchaifing either kept a relocation kit prepared in advance or commandeered one from the council's own emergency stores, which is even funnier. The harp was in her vault before anyone thought to ask whether it should be.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
